## Family assignments

<!-- agentkit:family-roster -->

Only parents listed in this workflow's family roster can delegate, and only to their own listed children. This exception applies once the main session has approved the parent's scope. A parent can handle a small task itself or choose installed children for bounded work. Children return evidence to the parent and cannot delegate. The main session may also assign any available role directly.

Use this installed Codex workflow as the source for dispatch. Before giving the parent its roster, filter the installed candidates against their current model, permissions, and registration. Apply the family launch checks below and pass only eligible roles. Verify that the parent and candidate files are still regular managed files under the active target, match their entries in that target's `agentkit/manifest.json`, and resolve to those roles in the running host. Repeat the eligibility check before launches and FIXes. A missing, edited, shadowed, excluded or otherwise ineligible role is unavailable for family routing.

- **Assignment** includes parent role, child role, objective, exact files (with read and write scope), inherited permissions and tools, and acceptance checks. Preserve the parent assignment's boundaries and user approvals. Security work is defensive, static and read-only. Testing edits are limited to assigned test files and use fake services.
- **Launch** uses the native host tool only when it can enforce the actual registration, exact model and effort, sandbox, tools and narrower scope. Otherwise the parent returns the exact child assignment to the main session. The main session checks the approved parent scope and installed route, then launches that child as its own worker if the same launch checks pass. If the child cannot run, the parent works within its own approved scope or reports the gap.
- **Permissions** for family dispatch must enforce the approved file and tool limits without widening the sandbox. An interface exposing only prompt, model and effort cannot enforce those limits. Reject family launches with ambiguous settings, permission bypass, `danger-full-access`, or an `agentkit:claude:start` or `agentkit:codex:start` relay.
- **Result** includes parent and child roles, child thread ID when available, files changed, actual check results and open gaps. The main session returns fallback results to the parent. The parent aggregates all results and gives a single report to the main session for `supervisor-review`.
- **FIX** goes through the same parent and child, with the earlier result and original scope. Use the same eligible thread when possible and the same checked fallback when needed. New scope needs main-session approval.

# Agent management (agentkit)
The shared agent roles are installed by agentkit. Each role has an [agents.*] entry in the active Codex configuration and a file in its agents directory. `agentkit update` replaces files that I did not change, and keeps files that I changed. When I ask to add a new agent role or change one, do it in those places, in English, with the same format as the other roles. Show me the change first. Write it after I approve. Update the role list above when a role is added or removed.
